  <p class="study-intro">A Words of Plainness Companion Study</p>

  <div class="decl-intro">
    <p>These declarations are written for the historic Christian families — the communions that confess the Nicene faith, together about 95 percent of Christians worldwide. Each one begins in the words of Jesus in the four gospels, the red letters supreme, and is worded at the level where agreement across these families is genuine, not nominal.</p>
    <p>Beneath each declaration a witness stack deepens the testimony from the wider canon without narrowing it; a reader space is left open for each tradition to fill from its own creed and commentary. All nineteen declarations clear the 80-percent threshold among the creedal families — including the full deity of Christ, the dogmatic center these families hold in common.</p>
    <p>An honest word about the numbers: no one can poll the living church. Every percentage here is an estimate grounded in documented confessional positions, not a measured statistic. Where an estimate is soft, the entry says so. The boundary list at the end is as much the point as the declarations — a shorter set of truly shared affirmations is worth more than a long list of forced ones.</p>
  </div>

  <details class="decl-method"><summary>How we built this — the method in seven phases</summary>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Harvest.</strong> Recurring teaching principles about Christ were drawn from the four gospels, red letters first, noting multi-gospel attestation.</li>
      <li><strong>Cluster.</strong> Principles were grouped into a candidate set; near-duplicates merged, and any item bundling a universal idea with a contested one was split.</li>
      <li><strong>Frame.</strong> Each declaration is worded at the level where affirmation is genuine, anchored in the words Jesus used; no post-biblical metaphysics was imported into the shared wording.</li>
      <li><strong>Build the witness stack.</strong> Tier 1 to Tier 2 to Tier 3 anchors were assembled beneath each declaration; Tier 3 corroborates only; contested-reading anchors are tagged; the Restoration layer is witness-only and never counts toward a rating.</li>
      <li><strong>Resolve from inside the gospels.</strong> Where a teaching is contested by interpretation, the meaning is resolved from another gospel passage where possible, not from the epistles.</li>
      <li><strong>Validate.</strong> For each tradition, the declaration as worded was assessed Affirm, Affirm-with-qualification, or Reject against that tradition&rsquo;s own confessional position.</li>
      <li><strong>Score and boundary-map.</strong> Agreement is estimated under the denominator in view, governed by the highest tier that still clears 80 percent; teachings that could not clear the bar are recorded honestly on the boundary list.</li>
    </ol>
  </details>

  <div class="study-divider">&#10022;&ensp;&ensp;&#10022;&ensp;&ensp;&#10022;</div>

  <h2 class="study-section-heading">The Declarations</h2>

<article class="decl-card" id="decl-01">
  <h3 class="decl-title"><span class="decl-num">01</span> The Two Great Commandments</h3>
  <blockquote class="decl-statement">We affirm that Jesus taught the love of God with all one&rsquo;s heart, soul, mind, and strength, and the love of one&rsquo;s neighbor as oneself, as the greatest commandments, on which all the Law and the Prophets depend.</blockquote>
  <p class="decl-rating"><span class="decl-pill decl-pill-pass">Widely shared</span> <span class="decl-pct">~99%</span> &mdash; No major confession contests this; affirmed as the summary of the moral law.</p>
  <details class="decl-witness"><summary>Show the witness</summary><div class="decl-witness-body">
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Tier 1 · red letter —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/matt/22?lang=eng&id=p37-p40#p37" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matthew 22:37-40</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/mark/12?lang=eng&id=p29-p31#p29" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mark 12:29-31</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/luke/10?lang=eng&id=p27#p27" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Luke 10:27</a> (triple-attested)</p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Tier 2 · gospel —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/luke/10?lang=eng&id=p29-p37#p29" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Luke 10:29-37</a> (the Good Samaritan — Jesus&rsquo;s own teaching defining &ldquo;neighbor&rdquo;)</p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Tier 3 · apostolic —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/rom/13?lang=eng&id=p9-p10#p9" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Romans 13:9-10</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/gal/5?lang=eng&id=p14#p14" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Galatians 5:14</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/james/2?lang=eng&id=p8#p8" target="_blank" rel="noopener">James 2:8</a> (corroboration)</p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Restoration —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/bofm/mosiah/2?lang=eng&id=p17#p17" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mosiah 2:17</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/dc-testament/dc/59?lang=eng&id=p5-p6#p5" target="_blank" rel="noopener">D&amp;C 59:5-6</a></p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Reader space —</strong> open</p>
    <hr class="decl-meta-rule">
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Governing tier.</strong> Tier 1 — holds on the red letters alone.</p>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Affirm / Qualify / Reject.</strong> Affirmed universally as a principle; no tradition rejects it as worded. Confessional sources: CCC §2055, §2083; Westminster Larger Catechism Q.102, Q.122; Baptist Faith &amp; Message 2000, Art. XV; LDS Articles of Faith 1:13.</p>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Interpretive divergence.</strong> Scope of &ldquo;neighbor&rdquo; (covenant community vs. universal) is resolved inside the gospels by the Good Samaritan, so no qualification is needed.</p>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Confidence.</strong> High.</p>
  </div></details>
</article>
<article class="decl-card" id="decl-02">
  <h3 class="decl-title"><span class="decl-num">02</span> The Golden Rule</h3>
  <blockquote class="decl-statement">We affirm that Jesus taught us to do to others as we would have them do to us, for this is the Law and the Prophets.</blockquote>
  <p class="decl-rating"><span class="decl-pill decl-pill-pass">Widely shared</span> <span class="decl-pct">~99%</span> &mdash; Universally affirmed; no documented rejection.</p>
  <details class="decl-witness"><summary>Show the witness</summary><div class="decl-witness-body">
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Tier 1 · red letter —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/matt/7?lang=eng&id=p12#p12" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matthew 7:12</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/luke/6?lang=eng&id=p31#p31" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Luke 6:31</a> (double-attested)</p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Tier 2 · gospel —</strong> —</p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Tier 3 · apostolic —</strong> —</p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Restoration —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/bofm/3-ne/14?lang=eng&id=p12#p12" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3 Nephi 14:12</a></p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Reader space —</strong> open</p>
    <hr class="decl-meta-rule">
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Governing tier.</strong> Tier 1.</p>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Affirm / Qualify / Reject.</strong> Affirmed universally. Confessional sources: Affirmed across the moral teaching of every tested family (CCC §1965–1974, the Law of the Gospel).</p>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Interpretive divergence.</strong> None of substance.</p>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Confidence.</strong> High.</p>
  </div></details>
</article>
<article class="decl-card" id="decl-03">
  <h3 class="decl-title"><span class="decl-num">03</span> Love Your Enemies and Pray for Persecutors</h3>
  <blockquote class="decl-statement">We affirm that Jesus taught us to love our enemies, to do good to those who hate us, to bless those who curse us, and to pray for those who persecute us, that we may be children of our Father in heaven.</blockquote>
  <p class="decl-rating"><span class="decl-pill decl-pill-pass">Widely shared</span> <span class="decl-pct">~94%</span> &mdash; Affirmed as Christ&rsquo;s explicit command across all families; only the application to force and defense diverges.</p>
  <p class="decl-readerspace"><strong>Left open for your tradition:</strong> <em>Whether the command requires absolute nonviolence or permits lawful defense and just-war reasoning belongs here.</em></p>
  <details class="decl-witness"><summary>Show the witness</summary><div class="decl-witness-body">
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Tier 1 · red letter —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/matt/5?lang=eng&id=p44-p45#p44" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matthew 5:44-45</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/luke/6?lang=eng&id=p27-p28,p35#p27" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Luke 6:27-28,35</a> (double-attested in the Sermon on the Mount and the Sermon on the Plain)</p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Tier 2 · gospel —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/matt/5?lang=eng&id=p46-p48#p46" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matthew 5:46-48</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/luke/23?lang=eng&id=p34#p34" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Luke 23:34</a> (Christ modeling the command from the cross)</p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Tier 3 · apostolic —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/rom/12?lang=eng&id=p14,p17-p21#p14" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Romans 12:14,17-21</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/1-pet/3?lang=eng&id=p9#p9" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1 Peter 3:9</a> (corroboration)</p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Restoration —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/bofm/3-ne/12?lang=eng&id=p44#p44" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3 Nephi 12:44</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/dc-testament/dc/98?lang=eng&id=p39-p40#p39" target="_blank" rel="noopener">D&amp;C 98:39-40</a></p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Reader space —</strong> <em>Whether the command requires absolute nonviolence or permits lawful defense and just-war reasoning belongs here.</em></p>
    <hr class="decl-meta-rule">
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Governing tier.</strong> Tier 1.</p>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Affirm / Qualify / Reject.</strong> Affirmed as worded by all. Anabaptist and Quaker traditions read it as binding nonresistance; Catholic, Orthodox, and magisterial Protestant traditions affirm the interpersonal ethic while permitting lawful defense and just war. Confessional sources: CCC §1825, §2844 (forgiveness and love of enemies), with legitimate-defense nuance at §2263–2267; Baptist Faith &amp; Message 2000, Art. XVI (Peace and War); Schleitheim Confession 1527, Art. VI (Anabaptist nonresistance).</p>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Interpretive divergence.</strong> Pacifism versus just war is a divergence about application, not a rejection of the words; the command to love and pray for enemies is shared.</p>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Confidence.</strong> High. High for the teaching; the divergence is about application, not assent.</p>
  </div></details>
</article>
<article class="decl-card" id="decl-04">
  <h3 class="decl-title"><span class="decl-num">04</span> Forgiveness Received and Extended</h3>
  <blockquote class="decl-statement">We affirm that Jesus taught us to forgive those who wrong us, and that the Father&rsquo;s forgiveness of us is bound up with our forgiveness of others.</blockquote>
  <p class="decl-rating"><span class="decl-pill decl-pill-pass">Widely shared</span> <span class="decl-pct">~98%</span> &mdash; The duty to forgive is affirmed across all families.</p>
  <details class="decl-witness"><summary>Show the witness</summary><div class="decl-witness-body">
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Tier 1 · red letter —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/matt/6?lang=eng&id=p14-p15#p14" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matthew 6:14-15</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/matt/18?lang=eng&id=p21-p22#p21" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matthew 18:21-22</a> (seventy times seven); <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/matt/18?lang=eng&id=p23-p35#p23" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matthew 18:23-35</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/mark/11?lang=eng&id=p25#p25" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mark 11:25</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/luke/6?lang=eng&id=p37#p37" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Luke 6:37</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/luke/17?lang=eng&id=p3-p4#p3" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Luke 17:3-4</a></p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Tier 2 · gospel —</strong> —</p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Tier 3 · apostolic —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/eph/4?lang=eng&id=p32#p32" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ephesians 4:32</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/col/3?lang=eng&id=p13#p13" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Colossians 3:13</a> (corroboration)</p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Restoration —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/bofm/3-ne/13?lang=eng&id=p14-p15#p14" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3 Nephi 13:14-15</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/dc-testament/dc/64?lang=eng&id=p9-p10#p9" target="_blank" rel="noopener">D&amp;C 64:9-10</a></p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Reader space —</strong> open</p>
    <hr class="decl-meta-rule">
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Governing tier.</strong> Tier 1.</p>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Affirm / Qualify / Reject.</strong> Affirmed universally. Some traditions stress that our forgiving is the evidence, not the cause, of pardon, but none reject the teaching. Confessional sources: CCC §2842–2845; Heidelberg Catechism Q.126; Westminster Shorter Catechism Q.105; Baptist Faith &amp; Message 2000, Art. IV.</p>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Interpretive divergence.</strong> Whether the conditionality (&ldquo;as we forgive&rdquo;) bears on assurance of salvation divides grace-and-works frameworks; the command is not in dispute.</p>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Confidence.</strong> High.</p>
  </div></details>
</article>
<article class="decl-card" id="decl-05">
  <h3 class="decl-title"><span class="decl-num">05</span> Care for the Least — Serving Christ in the Vulnerable</h3>
  <blockquote class="decl-statement">We affirm that Jesus taught that as we feed the hungry, give drink to the thirsty, welcome the stranger, clothe the naked, and visit the sick and imprisoned, we do it unto him.</blockquote>
  <p class="decl-rating"><span class="decl-pill decl-pill-pass">Widely shared</span> <span class="decl-pct">~97%</span> &mdash; The ethic of seeing Christ in the vulnerable is affirmed across all families.</p>
  <p class="decl-readerspace"><strong>Left open for your tradition:</strong> <em>Whether these deeds merit, evidence, or flow from saving faith, and whether &ldquo;the least of these&rdquo; means fellow disciples or all the vulnerable, belong here.</em></p>
  <details class="decl-witness"><summary>Show the witness</summary><div class="decl-witness-body">
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Tier 1 · red letter —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/matt/25?lang=eng&id=p31-p46#p31" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matthew 25:31-46</a></p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Tier 2 · gospel —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/mark/10?lang=eng&id=p21#p21" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mark 10:21</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/luke/14?lang=eng&id=p13-p14#p13" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Luke 14:13-14</a> (the ethic in action)</p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Tier 3 · apostolic —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/james/1?lang=eng&id=p27#p27" target="_blank" rel="noopener">James 1:27</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/1-jn/3?lang=eng&id=p17-p18#p17" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1 John 3:17-18</a> (corroboration)</p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Restoration —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/bofm/mosiah/2?lang=eng&id=p17#p17" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mosiah 2:17</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/bofm/mosiah/4?lang=eng&id=p16-p27#p16" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mosiah 4:16-27</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/bofm/alma/34?lang=eng&id=p28-p29#p28" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Alma 34:28-29</a></p>
