    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Tier 3 · apostolic —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/1-cor/11?lang=eng&id=p23-p26#p23" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1 Corinthians 11:23-26</a> (corroboration — Paul transmits the same institution and command to remember)</p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Restoration —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/bofm/3-ne/18?lang=eng&id=p1-p11#p1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3 Nephi 18:1-11</a>; Moroni 4-5; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/dc-testament/dc/20?lang=eng&id=p75-p79#p75" target="_blank" rel="noopener">D&amp;C 20:75-79</a></p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Reader space —</strong> <em>What the Supper IS — transubstantiation, sacramental union, pneumatic presence, Holy Mystery, or pure memorial — and whether it conveys grace belong here. Some groups (Quakers, the Salvation Army) do not observe it.</em></p>
    <hr class="decl-meta-rule">
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Governing tier.</strong> Tier 1 — at the level of institution and remembrance only. The presence question is reader space; it cannot be stated in shared wording without breaking consensus.</p>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Affirm / Qualify / Reject.</strong> Affirmed as worded (institution + remembrance) by nearly all; non-observing groups (Quakers, Salvation Army) and the depth of the presence dispute hold this at QUALIFIED. Confessional sources: transubstantiation — CCC §1373–1377 (Trent); sacramental union — Augsburg Confession Art. X, Formula of Concord VII; pneumatic presence — Westminster Confession ch. 29; &ldquo;cannot be proved by Holy Writ&rdquo; — Thirty-Nine Articles, Art. XXVIII; memorial — Baptist Faith &amp; Message 2000, Art. VII; not observed — Quaker and Salvation Army practice.</p>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Interpretive divergence.</strong> Real presence vs. memorial is the historic fault line; see the boundary list. The shared declaration deliberately states only what the red letters command: &ldquo;do this in remembrance of me.&rdquo;</p>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Confidence.</strong> Medium. Non-observing groups and the severity of the presence dispute make the rating a judgment call; the remembrance core is solid.</p>
    <p class="decl-meta decl-flag"><strong>Verification flag.</strong> The QUALIFIED rating is a judgment call weighing the non-observing groups (Quaker, Salvation Army) and the severity of the presence dispute; confirm both against primary confessions before wide distribution.</p>
  </div></details>
</article>
<article class="decl-card" id="decl-19">
  <h3 class="decl-title"><span class="decl-num">19</span> Jesus, the Son of God, One with the Father</h3>
  <blockquote class="decl-statement">We affirm that Jesus is the Son of God, sent from the Father, who said &ldquo;I and the Father are one&rdquo; and &ldquo;he who has seen me has seen the Father.&rdquo;</blockquote>
  <p class="decl-rating"><span class="decl-pill decl-pill-pass">Widely shared</span> <span class="decl-pct">~97%</span> &mdash; The deity of Christ is the dogmatic center of Nicene Christianity; affirmed by every historic family.</p>
  <p class="decl-readerspace"><strong>Left open for your tradition:</strong> <em>Nicene homoousios (&ldquo;of one substance&rdquo;), the metaphysics of the Trinity, and competing accounts of the Father-Son relation belong here.</em></p>
  <details class="decl-witness"><summary>Show the witness</summary><div class="decl-witness-body">
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Tier 1 · red letter —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/john/10?lang=eng&id=p30#p30" target="_blank" rel="noopener">John 10:30</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/john/14?lang=eng&id=p9-p11#p9" target="_blank" rel="noopener">John 14:9-11</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/john/8?lang=eng&id=p58#p58" target="_blank" rel="noopener">John 8:58</a> (&ldquo;before Abraham was, I am&rdquo;); <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/matt/11?lang=eng&id=p27#p27" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matthew 11:27</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/john/5?lang=eng&id=p17-p23#p17" target="_blank" rel="noopener">John 5:17-23</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/matt/16?lang=eng&id=p16-p17#p16" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matthew 16:16-17</a> (Jesus affirms Peter&rsquo;s confession); <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/john/17?lang=eng&id=p21-p22#p21" target="_blank" rel="noopener">John 17:21-22</a></p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Tier 2 · gospel —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/john/1?lang=eng&id=p1,p14,p18#p1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">John 1:1,14,18</a> (tagged — the prologue, &ldquo;the Word was God,&rdquo; unites the creedal core and strains the expanded tent); <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/john/20?lang=eng&id=p28#p28" target="_blank" rel="noopener">John 20:28</a> (Jesus receives Thomas&rsquo;s &ldquo;My Lord and my God&rdquo;)</p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Tier 3 · apostolic —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/col/1?lang=eng&id=p15-p20#p15" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Colossians 1:15-20</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/philip/2?lang=eng&id=p6-p11#p6" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Philippians 2:6-11</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/heb/1?lang=eng&id=p3,p8#p3" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Hebrews 1:3,8</a>; Titus 2:13 (corroboration; tagged — contested in expanded-tent readings)</p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Restoration —</strong> <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/bofm/3-ne/11?lang=eng&id=p7,p10-p11#p7" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3 Nephi 11:7,10-11</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/bofm/mosiah/15?lang=eng&id=p1-p4#p1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mosiah 15:1-4</a>; D&amp;C 76:22-24 (witness-only; note: the Restoration confesses Christ&rsquo;s divinity but as a distinct personage in a Godhead of three beings, not the Nicene one-substance)</p>
    <p class="decl-stack"><strong>Reader space —</strong> <em>Nicene homoousios (&ldquo;of one substance&rdquo;), the metaphysics of the Trinity, and competing accounts of the Father-Son relation belong here.</em></p>
    <hr class="decl-meta-rule">
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Governing tier.</strong> Tier 1/2 — the red-letter sayings and the gospel framing hold the deity of Christ outright; affirmed by every historic family.</p>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Affirm / Qualify / Reject.</strong> Creedal families: AFFIRM. Latter-day Saints: AFFIRM-WITH-QUALIFICATION (Jesus is divine and &ldquo;one&rdquo; with the Father in will and purpose; not one in substance — LDS Articles of Faith 1). Jehovah&rsquo;s Witnesses: REJECT (Watch Tower: Jesus is &ldquo;a god,&rdquo; not God Almighty, the archangel Michael). Unitarian Christians: REJECT. Confessional sources: Nicene Creed (homoousios); CCC §464–469 (true God and true man); Chalcedonian Definition; Thirty-Nine Articles, Art. II; Westminster Confession ch. 8; one in purpose, not substance — LDS Articles of Faith 1; a created being, not God Almighty — Watch Tower teaching.</p>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Interpretive divergence.</strong> Creedal traditions read &ldquo;I and the Father are one&rdquo; as unity of being; Latter-day Saints read it as unity of will; Jehovah&rsquo;s Witnesses read it as agency under a superior. The words are shared by most; the metaphysics is not.</p>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Confidence.</strong> High. This is the showcase of the two-axis method: a red-letter-grounded, high-authority teaching that sits squarely on a historic agreement fault line. The creedal PASS and expanded FAIL are both well-documented.</p>
  </div></details>
</article>

