  <h2 class="study-section-heading">The Boundary — What We Could Not Yet Share</h2>
  <p class="decl-intro"><em>Gospel teachings that could not clear the 80-percent bar as a joint declaration among the creedal families. Recorded plainly and unwatered — the boundary is honest ground, not failure.</em></p>

  <div class="decl-boundary">
  <div class="decl-boundary-item"><h4>01 — Baptismal regeneration; the necessity and mode of baptism</h4><p>Whether baptism regenerates, who may receive it (infants vs. believers only), its proper mode, and its necessity divide the sacramental families from most Baptists and Evangelicals — and Quakers and the Salvation Army do not practice water baptism at all.</p><p class="decl-boundary-refs"><a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/john/3?lang=eng&id=p5#p5" target="_blank" rel="noopener">John 3:5</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/matt/28?lang=eng&id=p19#p19" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matthew 28:19</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/mark/16?lang=eng&id=p16#p16" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mark 16:16</a></p></div>
  <div class="decl-boundary-item"><h4>02 — The real presence in the Eucharist</h4><p>The institution is shared (Declaration #18), but transubstantiation, sacramental union, pneumatic presence, and pure memorialism cannot be jointly affirmed; the meaning of &ldquo;this is my body&rdquo; is the deepest historic fault line of all.</p><p class="decl-boundary-refs"><a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/john/6?lang=eng&id=p53-p56#p53" target="_blank" rel="noopener">John 6:53-56</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/luke/22?lang=eng&id=p19#p19" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Luke 22:19</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/matt/26?lang=eng&id=p26#p26" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matthew 26:26</a></p></div>
  <div class="decl-boundary-item"><h4>03 — The nature of final punishment</h4><p>Eternal conscious torment (the historic majority), annihilation / conditional immortality (Adventists, Jehovah&rsquo;s Witnesses, some Evangelicals), and universal restoration cannot be jointly affirmed.</p><p class="decl-boundary-refs"><a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/matt/25?lang=eng&id=p46#p46" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matthew 25:46</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/mark/9?lang=eng&id=p43-p48#p43" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mark 9:43-48</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/matt/10?lang=eng&id=p28#p28" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matthew 10:28</a></p></div>
  <div class="decl-boundary-item"><h4>04 — The authority of the church; Peter and the keys</h4><p>Papal primacy (Catholic), conciliar-episcopal succession (Orthodox), and the priesthood of all believers (Protestant) read &ldquo;the keys&rdquo; and &ldquo;binding and loosing&rdquo; incompatibly.</p><p class="decl-boundary-refs"><a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/matt/16?lang=eng&id=p18-p19#p18" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matthew 16:18-19</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/matt/18?lang=eng&id=p18#p18" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matthew 18:18</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/john/20?lang=eng&id=p23#p23" target="_blank" rel="noopener">John 20:23</a></p></div>
  <div class="decl-boundary-item"><h4>05 — Marriage, divorce, and remarriage</h4><p>Indissolubility with annulment (Catholic), economia and permitted remarriage (Orthodox), and varied Protestant grounds for divorce are genuinely divisive. Included here unwatered, per the no-softening rule — the disagreement is real and the boundary is honest.</p><p class="decl-boundary-refs"><a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/matt/5?lang=eng&id=p31-p32#p31" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matthew 5:31-32</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/matt/19?lang=eng&id=p3-p9#p3" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matthew 19:3-9</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/mark/10?lang=eng&id=p11-p12#p11" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mark 10:11-12</a></p></div>
  <div class="decl-boundary-item"><h4>06 — The mode of Christ&rsquo;s second coming and millennial scheme</h4><p>The fact of the return and judgment is shared (Declaration #17); premillennial, amillennial, postmillennial, and preterist readings of how and when cannot be jointly affirmed.</p><p class="decl-boundary-refs"><a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/matt/24?lang=eng&id=p29-p31#p29" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matthew 24:29-31</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/matt/25?lang=eng&id=p31#p31" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matthew 25:31</a>; <a class="scripture-link" href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/rev/20?lang=eng&id=p1-p6#p1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Revelation 20:1-6</a></p></div>
  </div>

  <details class="decl-methodology"><summary>Methodology &amp; limits</summary>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Translation basis.</strong> Red letters were identified against public-domain baselines (KJV / World English Bible) with cross-checks. Where editions disagree on where Jesus&rsquo;s speech ends (e.g. John 3:16ff), the disputed verses were treated conservatively and no declaration leans on a contested attribution.</p>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Sources consulted.</strong> Confessional positions were drawn from the historic standards of the tested families: the Nicene and Apostles&rsquo; Creeds; the Catechism of the Catholic Church; Eastern Orthodox confessions; the Book of Concord; the Westminster, Heidelberg, and Belgic standards; the Thirty-Nine Articles; the Baptist Faith &amp; Message; the Wesleyan Articles of Religion; classic Pentecostal statements; Stone-Campbell and Anabaptist positions; the Seventh-day Adventist Fundamental Beliefs; and, for the expanded tent, the Latter-day Saint Articles of Faith and Watch Tower doctrinal statements. The eucharistic-presence spectrum, expanded-tent Christology, and the views of final punishment were additionally checked against current comparative sources.</p>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>What the estimates can and cannot do.</strong> The figures distinguish broad consensus from contested ground; they cannot stand as measured data. Medium-confidence ratings turn on a single tradition&rsquo;s qualification and are flagged as such. Three declarations carry an explicit verification flag — the new birth, the gift of the Spirit, and the Lord&rsquo;s Supper — marking ratings that should be confirmed against the named confessions before wide distribution. The Restoration witness is included throughout as witness-only and never affects a rating, because most Christian traditions do not receive that canon.</p>
    <p class="decl-meta"><strong>Style.</strong> &ldquo;Latter-day Saint,&rdquo; not &ldquo;Mormon,&rdquo; except in historical quotation; em-dashes per Chicago; scripture hyperlinked to churchofjesuschrist.org/study.</p>
  </details>

